ForGoodTech log4php
===================

This repository is a narrowly maintained PHP 8 compatibility fork of Apache
log4php 2.3.0. It exists to support legacy ForGoodTech applications while they
migrate to a maintained PSR-3 logger. New features are out of scope.

The maintained line supports the currently supported PHP 8.2 through PHP 8.5
branches. Every release is tested against each of those versions.

Install a tagged release with Composer:

    composer require forgoodtech/log4php:^2.3.1

Load the generated autoloader before configuring the logger:

    require_once __DIR__ . '/vendor/autoload.php';
    Logger::configure(__DIR__ . '/p/log4php_daily.xml');

Applications should commit their own composer.json and composer.lock files,
exclude vendor/ from source control, and include the generated vendor/ tree in
each deployment artifact. Production servers do not need Composer or network
access.

Upstream
========

Apache log4php is a versatile logging framework for PHP.

Apache log4php is a project at the Apache Software Foundation (ASF).

Project web site: 
http://logging.apache.org/log4php/

Project Status
==============
Apache log4php graduated from the Apache Incubator in March 2010 and entered
dormant status in December 2020. This fork is maintained independently by
ForGoodTech and is not an Apache Software Foundation project.
